# Build context hygiene: images are built from the repo root.
# NOTE: .git/ is intentionally NOT ignored — the app image derives the product
# version from `git describe` in its build stage (ci.md, 1.T4). It stays in the
# build stage only (multi-stage); the final image carries just the version string.
.devcontainer/
docs/
docs-ita/
backups/
compose*.yml
# Match at ANY depth: the real one is src/frontend/node_modules (~109MB, tens of
# thousands of files). A bare `node_modules/` only matches the (non-existent) root
# one, so BuildKit would still walk the nested tree on every build (slow on the
# Windows mount). The frontend stage rebuilds it with `npm ci` anyway.
**/node_modules/
src/frontend/.svelte-kit/
src/frontend/build/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
.env
# Not used by any build stage — kept out of the context so they aren't shipped to
# the daemon on every build (the app image never COPYies these).
tests/
.github/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.env.example
